course: dictionary
lesson: 6713
title: Feeling offended
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Offended means feeling hurt, upset or insulted by what someone said or did. When you meet it in a story, look at what happened just before. «The Mouse swam away offended» tells you the Mouse was upset, so it left the conversation.
explain: The words around a word are its clues. In «I mean what I say,» answers the Mock Turtle, offended, the word offended tells you how he feels about what Alice said. Ask yourself what would make someone feel that way, then swap in upset or hurt and check the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Offended can also be the past form of offend, which means to upset someone. «You're so easily offended, you know!» means Alice thinks the Mouse gets upset too quickly. When you see «take offence» or «be offended by», look at what comes after to find out what caused the feeling.
fact: Offended means feeling hurt, upset or insulted.
fact: «Offended» is the past form of offend, which means to make someone upset.
fact: «Easily offended» means quick to feel upset.
fact: In formal English, offend can also mean to break a law.
fact: Useful phrases: take offence, be offended by, look offended.
exercise: «The Mouse swam away offended.» What does offended mean here? | Happy and excited | Very tired from swimming | Lost in the water | *Upset and hurt
exercise: Alice says, «you're so easily offended, you know!» What does easily offended mean? | *Quick to feel upset | Slow to notice anything | Never sad | Good at swimming
exercise: Which phrase means to become upset by something someone said? | *Take offence | Take a nap | Take care | Take the bus
test: «I mean what I say,» answers the Mock Turtle, offended. How does the Mock Turtle feel? | Lost | *Upset at what Alice said | Delighted with the tea | Sleepy and calm
test: «The joke offended Sam.» What did the joke do? | Made Sam hungry | Made Sam laugh | Made Sam tired | *Made Sam upset
exam: «Every time she tries to make friends she makes it worse, until the Mouse swims away offended.» Why did the Mouse swim away? | Because it wanted to find Dinah | Because it wanted a swim | *Because it felt hurt and upset | Because it was hungry
